//@version=6
indicator("Rexercise | GTOP Ribbon + Ranges v2.1", shorttitle="GTOP v2.1", overlay=true, scale=scale.none, max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=50, behind_chart=true)

// INSTALL: Paste into a NEW TradingView Pine indicator, save, and Add to chart.
// v2.1 matches Rexercise's higher hand-drawn ribbon: one continuous, soft-color
// row under the candles, including the overnight Not The Job bridge. Defaults
// show the current block through its scheduled end, without projecting the
// rest of the day. Oct 5's green The Job is the supplied MANUAL annotation;
// other dates stay neutral. Change/reset that dated bias in Inputs as needed.
// v2.0 adds a user-selected monthly > weekly > daily > H4 context stack.
// Anchor relevance, objectives and narrative are manual; no automatic Butterfly
// detection or probability claim. Source OHLC uses confirmed full candle ranges.
// The compact chart drawing is retained: a slim, light time-aligned strip
// inside the PRICE chart. Its blocks use real New York timestamps and move
// with candles when scrolling/zooming. No fixed-screen table or separate pane.
// If updating a pane-based version, remove/re-add this chart instance so the
// overlay setting takes effect. Existing manual chart drawings are untouched.
// Ribbon vertical placement uses the visible candles' high/low range. It
// rebuilds when the horizontal viewport changes; vertical-only price panning
// moves it with the price chart. Height and gap are adjustable in Inputs.
// v1.3 safeguards retained: sample confirmation, missing-data coverage,
// right-edge intrabar ranges, DST-safe overnight anchoring, zoom-aware labels.
// Standard charts: monthly/weekly/daily for context, 1m-4h for shift execution.
// On higher chart timeframes, intraday ribbons/range engines are suppressed.
// Use TradingView price-scale menu > Scale price chart only to keep distant
// monthly objectives from squeezing the intraday candles.
// Model1 is explicitly selected and linked to a selected CRT anchor. CISD uses
// only an assigned-timeframe confirmed close strictly beyond its FULL high/low.
// Bias is MANUAL, not a signal: each dropdown recolors that recurring slot.
// Optional selected-date scope leaves all other dates neutral.
// Range highs/lows use available chart-session data. Missing opening data is
// marked PARTIAL. Developing ranges change until their time window finishes.
// On bars crossing a range boundary, 1m/5m intrabars prevent including prices
// from outside that range. Older intrabars can be unavailable on TradingView;
// the chart warns and affected ranges are omitted/marked PARTIAL, not guessed.
// Completed values are frozen. No trading, orders, or automatic CRT claims.

// SETTINGS -------------------------------------------------------------------
string G_STACK = "00 | Top-down GTOP context"
bool stackOn = input.bool(true, "Selected context stack", group=G_STACK)
